There is *a lot* to cover in this release, and I'm not a little proud to share it with you! Much thanks to Keystone, a good friend, for working through a lot of backend behavior and objects with me. Without their testing, I'd be exhausted.


## Editing

- The NoteTab toolbar now has a button for embedding images. Pasting via keyboard shortcut is no longer the only way to insert an image.

- Users can now double-click on images in order to expand them in a view. This view supports zooming, panning, and exporting the image to a file. It snaps to sticky notes, as well.


## Files

- Autosaving is now handled via *delta files*: Instead of autosaving the entire database, we now save only changes that were made in the current session. This saves massively on file space, and takes far less work.

- There are now menu options in the File menu for browsing the database and backup folders.

- Backups are now stored in the user's AppData/Local folder, instead of alongside the main database files.

- A longstanding bug preventing opening SIDB files by clicking on them has been finally fixed.

- Better file safety and sharing should now prevent rare errors when saving a database to a file.


## Language

- For multilingual users, a niche bug has been fixed which would have caused filename conflicts when switching the OS display language.


## Themes

- An **Ice** theme has been added to the predefined list. It's a bright light-mode selection that fills in a niche the existing set didn't have. Users who rely on bright aesthetics for vision or focus will have a much easier time now!

